Description: The biomastat package provides tools for loading, analyzing, and visualizing time series data of land use and coverage in Brazilian territory. The package includes functions for data downloading, preprocessing, visualization, and statistical analysis to gain insights into land use patterns and trends: areas, landscape and fragment metrics, class diversity, time-series regimes, land change, class adjacency and fragment connectivity. Optional external layers (ESA WorldCover, OpenStreetMap, Overture Maps, Copernicus DEM and SoilGrids) are aligned to the same study area. The land use data are sourced from MapBiomas Project - Collection 10 of the Annual Series of Land Use and Land Cover Maps of Brazil (1985-2024), available at https://mapbiomas.org/colecoes-mapbiomas-1. The MapBiomas data is public, open, and freely available under the Creative Commons CC-BY-SA license, with attribution to the data source required (Souza et al., 2020).
